mode: "100644"
text: "# The Growth Engine\n\nHow Instagram growth actually works in 2026 — the model everything else in this skill builds on. Get\nthis right and the tactics follow; get it wrong and you optimize the wrong things.\n\n> Platform behavior changes — re-verify quarterly. The direction (discovery-first, sends + watch\n> time, multiple algorithms) has been steady and confirmed by Instagram's own statements.\n\n## Instagram is a discovery engine, not a follower feed\n\nThe single most important shift: the vast majority of reach now comes from **non-followers** via\n**Reels and Explore** — roughly **94% of distribution is AI recommendations**, not your follower\ngraph. So **reach is earned per post, not borrowed from your follower count.** Follower count is a\nlagging vanity number; **reach, sends, saves, and profile visits** are what move.\n\n## The three signals that matter (confirmed by Instagram)\n\nAcross surfaces, Instagram's head has confirmed the top ranking signals:\n\n1. **Watch time** — the single most important signal, especially on Reels. The **first ~3 seconds**\n   decide whether a Reel is pushed wider or throttled. Completion and **rewatches** are strong.\n2. **Sends per reach (DM shares)** — the dominant signal for **reaching new people**; weighted\n   **~3–5× more than likes** for discovery. (Its own reference: `the-sends-lever.md`.)\n3. **Likes per reach** — still counts, but matters more for **existing followers** than for\n   discovery.\n\nThe practical read: **strong hook (watch time) + send-worthy content (sends)** is the combination\nthat travels.\n\n## Multiple algorithms — one per surface\n\nThere isn't one algorithm; each surface ranks differently. Match the content to the surface's signal:\n\n| Surface | What it rewards | Its job |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Reels** | watch time, rewatches, **sends**, audio fit, low skip | **discovery / growth** (mostly non-followers) |\n| **Feed** | relationship, saves, comments, profile taps, time spent | reach **existing followers** |\n| **Stories** | closeness, replies, recency | **retention / relationship** (followers only) |\n| **Explore** | topic match, non-follower engagement velocity, freshness, **DM shares from non-followers** | **discovery** (all non-followers) |\n\nA Reel can go wide on the Reels tab and barely show in Feed — that's not a contradiction, it's\ndifferent surfaces doing different jobs.\n\n## Connected vs unconnected reach\n\nOptimize the two reach types differently:\n\n- **Unconnected (discovery / new people):** shareability (**sends**), hook strength, watch time,\n  trending audio, niche clarity. This is where you *grow*. Newer accounts should skew **~70/30 toward\n  unconnected-reach tactics** until they build an audience.\n- **Connected (your followers):** consistency, community, fast replies, saves/comments, Stories\n  relationship. This *retains* and warms the audience, which boosts early signals on new posts.\n\n## The growth loop\n\n```\nReels/Explore reach non-followers  →  strong hook holds them (watch time)\n        →  content is send-worthy (sends)  →  Instagram pushes it wider\n        →  viewer taps the profile  →  profile converts to a follow\n        →  Stories/Feed/community deepen the relationship (retention)\n        →  warm followers boost early signals on the next post  →  more reach\n```\n\nEvery growth problem is a **specific broken stage** in this loop (see `format-and-diagnosis.md`).\nDiagnose the stage; don't apply random tips.\n\n## The eligibility gates (before ranking even happens)\n\nTo be eligible for recommendations (Explore, non-follower Reels), content must clear gates:\n\n- **Original** — reposts get far less distribution; heavy reposting (e.g., 10+ in 30 days) can\n  **exclude the account from recommendations** entirely.\n- **No other-platform watermarks** (TikTok/CapCut logos) — a common, avoidable growth killer.\n- **Has audio, under the length cap** (Reels up to ~3 min are now eligible for non-follower reach,\n  though ~30–90s often performs best), and **suitable/safe** for a broad audience.\n\nMade-for-Instagram, original, watermark-free is the price of entry for reach.\n\n## Trial Reels (a free growth tool)\n\nInstagram lets you post a **Trial Reel** shown **only to non-followers** first. If it performs with a\ncold audience, push it to your followers; if not, you learn at no cost to your follower-facing stats.\nUse it to test hooks/formats/topics risk-free.\n"
